<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Caucasian War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1817–1864</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Caucasian War was the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a>'s long conquest of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-caucasus">North Caucasus</a>, from 1817 to 1864. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> faced fierce resistance from the peoples of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chechnya">Chechnya</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dagestan">Dagestan</a>, united under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imam-shamil">Imam Shamil</a> until his surrender in 1859, and from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/circassians">Circassians</a> in the north-west, whose defeat in 1864 was followed by the mass expulsion of Circassians to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/caucasian-war.jpg" alt="Caucasian War" width="320" height="210" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Franz Roubaud · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Roubaud._Scene_from_Caucasian_war.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
